Z||000003||pollock||09-29-2000||09:31 AM||||Don't know if this is still true, but a year or two ago it was....<P>The fastest Dodge is obviously the Viper.  Know what #2 is?<P><BR>......Neon R/T.<P>Sorry you're frustrated dude.  Fact is, you can't rely 100% on what you read here.  Everybody on this forum blows his share of smoke from time to time, and you're right.... there is some flat-out BSing.  <P>The most forthcoming source of 3.8 info is on a page called Dancar Motorsports.  He did the swap himself and isn't looking to make any money by telling you what he learned.  <P>Don't worry.  I'm sure you'll get there.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||3400Fiero||09-29-2000||09:44 AM||||I have never been smoked by a neon since I put in my 3400DOHC.  I have smoked a few neons, however!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>To tell you the truth I now think they are small time.  It is hard for me to believe that a properly set up 3800 n/a would get beat by a neon.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Both 3800 s/c and 350 should eat neons for lunch! <P>------------------<BR>1988 Fiero 3400DOHC<BR>||||reg||1
