Z||000007||ThatRickGuy||09-29-2000||01:15 PM||||I'm gonna agree with 3400 on this one, a properly set up 3.8 fiero should be able to at least keep up w/ a neon. With a little work, you should be able to burn him. The only thing I could set it how specifically you set you car up. A stock 2.8 should take a neon off the line, just a mater of torque, but the neon has the top end advantage. So, learn where your car performs the best. In my 3.2 conversion, I'm building for toque, so I'll keep most of my 'races' at lower speed and use the handling and quick acceleration to win, but out on the highway, it'll be just like that other person said, I could be going 100 and the would just pull away.||||reg||1
